709
00:53:00,432 --> 00:53:02,372
[SPEAKER_17]: that you may have fall on the presentation tonight.

710
00:53:07,893 --> 00:53:17,095
[SPEAKER_17]: Um, so we'll, we'll be starting with, uh, some zoning variances that the project will be seeking and how our team got here this evening is, is really where I'm I'll be starting.

711
00:53:17,155 --> 00:53:19,935
[SPEAKER_17]: So about a year ago, rise partnered with the moderate.

712
00:53:19,955 --> 00:53:21,736
[SPEAKER_17]: So family to reimagine this site.

713
00:53:22,156 --> 00:53:29,117
[SPEAKER_17]: Uh, the family has owned the site for decades and is excited to be working on bringing a project such as this to the city of Medford.

714
00:53:31,568 --> 00:53:41,371
[SPEAKER_17]: As we continue working with the Matarazzo family, we realized quickly we needed a truly special project team to bring life science into the city of Medford.

715
00:53:41,431 --> 00:53:44,652
[SPEAKER_17]: So for architecture, we have Cube 3 and Jacobs.

716
00:53:45,232 --> 00:53:49,053
[SPEAKER_17]: For civil engineering, as well as permitting and transportation, we have VHB.

717
00:53:49,914 --> 00:53:52,414
[SPEAKER_17]: And for our landscape architects, we have MDLA.

718
00:53:53,035 --> 00:54:00,937
[SPEAKER_17]: And this team was really thought out very well by the project team here, because a lot of these team members have experience in the city of Medford.

719
00:54:01,435 --> 00:54:04,637
[SPEAKER_17]: but also are the experts in their field in the life science industry.

720
00:54:05,317 --> 00:54:09,200
[SPEAKER_17]: So we really think we have a great team here, all of whom are on the call tonight as well.

721
00:54:12,422 --> 00:54:17,625
[SPEAKER_17]: And once the team was assembled, we began researching the site's history and what was going on in the area today.

722
00:54:18,025 --> 00:54:26,590
[SPEAKER_17]: The site has been primarily marshlands up until the 1930s when it became a commercial use as Ralph's Potato factory and laboratory.

723
00:54:27,898 --> 00:54:31,560
[SPEAKER_17]: In the 1990s, Bertucci's took over the site and still operates there today.

724
00:54:32,961 --> 00:54:35,882
[SPEAKER_17]: Around the site, we saw many ongoing initiatives in the city.

725
00:54:36,242 --> 00:54:44,987
[SPEAKER_17]: The Wellington Circle study was and is working on ways to make significant improvements in the intersection just down the street.

726
00:54:45,867 --> 00:54:51,890
[SPEAKER_17]: Local nonprofits are working to improve access and connectivity to the Tobrick MacDonald Park across the street from us.

727
00:54:52,733 --> 00:54:59,376
[SPEAKER_17]: And as we all are aware, the city of Medford is working through a comprehensive planning initiative that will shape the future of the neighborhood.

728
00:55:00,216 --> 00:55:05,038
[SPEAKER_17]: And for these reasons and more, the project team landed on life science as the best use for the site.

729
00:55:05,618 --> 00:55:16,142
[SPEAKER_17]: Life science allows us to protect the allowed commercial use of the site while supporting important local and regional initiatives and boosting economic development for the city of Medford.

730
00:55:19,940 --> 00:55:32,249
[SPEAKER_17]: And after we landed on that, and as the project team started designing the best use for the site, really what we've done over the past year is meet with numerous city and state agencies and local organizations.

731
00:55:32,929 --> 00:55:35,171
[SPEAKER_17]: You can see here a long list of meetings.

732
00:55:35,231 --> 00:55:38,693
[SPEAKER_17]: This is really just a short list of the meetings.

733
00:55:38,773 --> 00:55:45,378
[SPEAKER_17]: I actually couldn't fit most of them on here, but we've worked through multiple different processes and with multiple different

734
00:55:48,223 --> 00:55:52,868
[SPEAKER_17]: through the MEPA process and began conversations with MassDEP and MassDOT.

735
00:55:53,509 --> 00:56:01,236
[SPEAKER_17]: We've had community meetings and conversations with groups such as the Chamber of Commerce, the Mystic River Watershed Association, and Medford High School.

736
00:56:01,917 --> 00:56:09,925
[SPEAKER_17]: And just last week, we wrapped up the Medford's Community Development Board process, who issued their order of conditions and recommendations thereafter.

737
00:56:14,048 --> 00:56:18,790
[SPEAKER_17]: All of this work resulted in many improvements and benefits that we've been able to add to the project.

738
00:56:19,511 --> 00:56:27,714
[SPEAKER_17]: We're implementing important civil engineering designs that will significantly improve stormwater management on our site and to surrounding sites.

739
00:56:28,655 --> 00:56:33,197
[SPEAKER_17]: Our design team continues to progress toward efficiency and sustainability goals.

740
00:56:33,957 --> 00:56:40,220
[SPEAKER_17]: Traffic improvements and TDM measures will mitigate impacts and support connections within the surrounding area.

741
00:56:41,190 --> 00:56:47,455
[SPEAKER_17]: We're providing new public realm improvements and community space at the front edge and on the ground floor of the project.

742
00:56:48,236 --> 00:56:58,083
[SPEAKER_17]: And we're continuing to work with Medford Vocational Technical High School on partnerships to support their student body and we're hoping to start those in the fall of 2022 this year.

743
00:56:58,724 --> 00:57:00,145
[SPEAKER_17]: Really excited initiative there.

744
00:57:01,356 --> 00:57:12,706
[SPEAKER_17]: The project today and its benefits to the city of Medford were all made possible through these collaborations and processes with these groups and organizations and are truly going to transform this site into its best use.

745
00:57:13,506 --> 00:57:18,731
[SPEAKER_17]: We're excited to continue working with these groups and the ZBA tonight to bring this project to life for Medford.

746
00:57:19,191 --> 00:57:22,134
