[SPEAKER_10]: Thank you, Chair.

851
01:10:09,808 --> 01:10:12,610
[SPEAKER_10]: This is Victor Schrader, Economic Development Director for the city.

852
01:10:12,731 --> 01:10:21,178
[SPEAKER_10]: I actually just have a short bit of background on the project that I think might be valuable to the board.

853
01:10:21,518 --> 01:10:28,885
[SPEAKER_10]: I've been working with RISE for about a year, and knowing projects like this come to communities you're never

854
01:10:29,485 --> 01:10:31,066
[SPEAKER_10]: quite sure how they're going to be received.

855
01:10:31,106 --> 01:10:33,428
[SPEAKER_10]: This is a pretty new use for Medford.

856
01:10:34,248 --> 01:10:46,217
[SPEAKER_10]: Modern Lab is of a specific size and scale and use that is unique and we don't really have any buildings like this in the city.

857
01:10:47,177 --> 01:10:53,161
[SPEAKER_10]: In addition, this project was pretty highly publicized from day one both locally and regionally.

858
01:10:54,142 --> 01:10:54,763
[SPEAKER_10]: RISE held a

859
01:10:55,952 --> 01:10:59,157
[SPEAKER_10]: A neighborhood meeting last fall that was very well attended.

860
01:10:59,177 --> 01:11:05,007
[SPEAKER_10]: They've also held three hearings before the city board recently.

861
01:11:06,065 --> 01:11:12,048
[SPEAKER_10]: And I think it's worth noting that there really has been no opposition to this project at all.

862
01:11:12,228 --> 01:11:23,473
[SPEAKER_10]: In fact, I've been doing this job similar to this for in order of 12 years, and this has probably been the least controversial project I've ever been a part of.

863
01:11:23,593 --> 01:11:26,114
[SPEAKER_10]: It's pretty amazing.

864
01:11:26,154 --> 01:11:29,916
[SPEAKER_10]: And I think credit for that goes to the RISE team.

865
01:11:29,936 --> 01:11:30,996
[SPEAKER_10]: They've been a great partner.

866
01:11:31,016 --> 01:11:34,278
[SPEAKER_10]: They've really gone above and beyond in terms of

867
01:11:35,417 --> 01:11:38,961
[SPEAKER_10]: design and working with the community and being responsive.

868
01:11:40,123 --> 01:11:41,965
[SPEAKER_10]: They see an opportunity for the site.

869
01:11:42,365 --> 01:11:45,349
[SPEAKER_10]: And that's similar to that the city does.

870
01:11:46,990 --> 01:11:50,254
[SPEAKER_10]: But I think also we'd like to credit the community.

871
01:11:50,915 --> 01:11:54,559
[SPEAKER_10]: We've just heard a lot of positive responses from the community.

872
01:11:55,460 --> 01:12:05,948
[SPEAKER_10]: regarding this project, the types of mitigation the project will be contributing, the design, the need for this type of development.

873
01:12:08,369 --> 01:12:16,695
[SPEAKER_10]: Even in addition at a recent visioning process or visioning session for the comprehensive plan,

874
01:12:18,584 --> 01:12:32,557
[SPEAKER_10]: the response from the community, there were probably 30 or 40 people on that call, was for dense mixed-use development with quality design and uses that bring life and vibrancy to the street.

875
01:12:32,637 --> 01:12:37,481
[SPEAKER_10]: So that really encompasses this project.

876
01:12:37,541 --> 01:12:40,644
[SPEAKER_10]: It's accomplishing all of these objectives in our mind.

877
01:12:41,785 --> 01:12:41,985
[SPEAKER_10]: But

878
01:12:43,006 --> 01:13:02,075
[SPEAKER_10]: Unfortunately, Medford zoning doesn't make approving these projects easy, as we know, it's the variance processes is challenging and as we've seen with a couple of what we think are really strong projects on Boston Avenue, Cummings and 590 Titan gas.

879
01:13:05,353 --> 01:13:09,234
[SPEAKER_10]: you know those projects weren't approved and we're not sure if they're going to come back.

880
01:13:09,254 --> 01:13:18,176
[SPEAKER_10]: I mean costs are going up these projects just get more and more challenging as time goes on because delays are poses significant risks.

881
01:13:18,236 --> 01:13:21,356
[SPEAKER_10]: It makes projects really expensive and challenges feasibility.

882
01:13:22,857 --> 01:13:28,558
[SPEAKER_10]: I think the moral of the story here is and we've heard we've heard this from the community and

883
01:13:29,638 --> 01:13:39,122
[SPEAKER_10]: and from the CD board as well, is that the city recognizes that we're really playing catch up when it comes to planning and zoning reform.

884
01:13:39,142 --> 01:13:40,462
[SPEAKER_10]: We're working on that.

885
01:13:41,643 --> 01:13:52,327
[SPEAKER_10]: When projects come to the city that are strong like this one, we wish we had a kind of an easier process than the variance process for them.

886
01:13:52,967 --> 01:13:55,768
[SPEAKER_10]: to take advantage of and I hope in the future that we do.

887
01:13:56,809 --> 01:14:07,513
[SPEAKER_10]: But tonight RISE is here to present their hardships and we just wanted to make sure that you're aware of the merits of the project and that the city and community are really supportive.

888
01:14:07,693 --> 01:14:08,914
[SPEAKER_10]: So thank you.

889
01:14:09,454 --> 01:14:10,354
[SPEAKER_04]: Great thank you so much.

