1402
02:04:56,542 --> 02:04:57,662
[SPEAKER_19]: City Council, not us.

1403
02:04:58,857 --> 02:05:03,959
[SPEAKER_19]: we can grant relief when the zoning's problematic.

1404
02:05:04,039 --> 02:05:09,742
[SPEAKER_19]: And I do think that the applicant has made some good points in that dimension.

1405
02:05:09,762 --> 02:05:25,128
[SPEAKER_19]: So regardless of, like, there's potentially a path here to a variance, but I do just want to say kind of on record, I think that probably the happy path or like the cleanest thing in the current zoning would just be say, hey, you know what, 02 is,

1406
02:05:27,001 --> 02:05:30,483
[SPEAKER_19]: Um, office slash R and D. It allows this use.

1407
02:05:31,403 --> 02:05:35,505
[SPEAKER_19]: It has the provision for the height, like it's cleaner.

1408
02:05:35,745 --> 02:05:43,389
[SPEAKER_19]: But with that being said, I do find the arguments related to the, uh,

1409
02:05:44,268 --> 02:05:46,910
[SPEAKER_19]: Marshall Ian precedent to be compelling.

1410
02:05:47,051 --> 02:06:07,869
[SPEAKER_19]: I do think that if you were to restrict the height to the the two stories I mean that's going to be a massive massive change in the economic liability of any project for any use and then furthermore wasn't referenced by the applicant, but

1411
02:06:09,268 --> 02:06:27,536
[SPEAKER_19]: There is another case, North Cross Virginia Board of Appeals, Boston, essentially where a height variance was upheld for a hotel that exceeded the height limits of the area on a high value parcel.

1412
02:06:28,596 --> 02:06:36,599
[SPEAKER_19]: So I'm not really going to speak to the full applicability of that case, but I do think there's some precedent out there for this.

1413
02:06:38,937 --> 02:06:40,039
[SPEAKER_19]: Yeah, and then let's see.

1414
02:06:40,900 --> 02:06:44,526
[SPEAKER_19]: Lastly, so I just want to make sure we touch on all the variances.

1415
02:06:44,606 --> 02:06:51,898
[SPEAKER_19]: So very clear to me from the applicant's petition that

1416
02:06:53,026 --> 02:07:03,895
