[SPEAKER_04]: Yeah.

1723
02:27:01,503 --> 02:27:04,025
[SPEAKER_04]: I have a kind of random question.

1724
02:27:04,085 --> 02:27:06,627
[SPEAKER_04]: I don't know if anyone has any thoughts on this.

1725
02:27:07,028 --> 02:27:14,754
[SPEAKER_04]: Typically at the meetings, I try to refer to people by their like formal names, but I don't want to be guessing at anyone's gender.

1726
02:27:14,794 --> 02:27:19,657
[SPEAKER_04]: Does anyone know of a good word to use instead of saying Mr. or Ms.?

1727
02:27:21,279 --> 02:27:22,199
[SPEAKER_04]: First names are fine with me.

1728
02:27:23,235 --> 02:27:25,636
[SPEAKER_04]: Yeah, I mean, maybe I don't need to be as formal.

1729
02:27:25,676 --> 02:27:33,058
[SPEAKER_04]: I just usually refer to like the neighbors who come in or anyone from the city by their, their like, I guess, proper names.

1730
02:27:34,998 --> 02:27:37,179
[SPEAKER_02]: Preferred pronouns are usually just asked.

1731
02:27:38,259 --> 02:27:48,962
[SPEAKER_02]: So if you have anybody's question, it always best practice to ask versus kind of a lot of Yeah, I just realized tonight when I was talking to people, I was saying Mr. or Ms.

1732
02:27:49,022 --> 02:27:50,583
[SPEAKER_04]: Then I was like, I don't know if that's even

1733
02:27:52,598 --> 02:27:53,738
[SPEAKER_04]: Maybe I'll just have to use first names.

1734
02:27:53,758 --> 02:27:54,919
[SPEAKER_04]: I'll get used to being informal.

1735
02:27:56,159 --> 02:27:57,919
[SPEAKER_04]: You can always offer them in there.

1736
02:27:58,319 --> 02:27:59,680
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah, in their signatures as well.

1737
02:28:00,180 --> 02:28:05,781
[SPEAKER_02]: You can always offer at the beginning of the meeting if folks wanna input that in their name change at the bottom.

1738
02:28:06,401 --> 02:28:07,001
[SPEAKER_26]: Oh, good idea.

1739
02:28:07,522 --> 02:28:07,822
[SPEAKER_26]: Okay.

1740
02:28:08,682 --> 02:28:09,462
[SPEAKER_02]: That's a great suggestion.

1741
02:28:12,583 --> 02:28:13,483
[SPEAKER_26]: I don't have anything else.

1742
02:28:14,083 --> 02:28:15,963
[SPEAKER_02]: Talk about things like that more at the training too.

1743
02:28:16,304 --> 02:28:21,025
[SPEAKER_02]: So that being said, I think it would be a good idea if folks in-house just automatically did that

1744
02:28:23,327 --> 02:28:32,234
[SPEAKER_02]: being prompted, so changing it in your profile on the Zoom account might be good practice.

1745
02:28:33,115 --> 02:28:38,099
[SPEAKER_02]: And to set an example so you wouldn't have to remind folks at the beginning of the meeting if you forgot.

1746
02:28:38,840 --> 02:28:39,280
[SPEAKER_02]: Great idea.

1747
02:28:40,839 --> 02:28:47,263
[SPEAKER_19]: Um, so we do have two items on the agenda that may be things we just pass through.

